// Copy this file to ios/Flutter/GoogleSignIn.xcconfig and fill in the values
// from your own Google Cloud project. The real file is git-ignored: these IDs
// belong to one project and one app signing identity, not to the repository.
//
// Do not quote the values and do not add spaces around `=`; Xcode reads this
// as build settings, and Info.plist substitutes them into GIDClientID,
// GIDServerClientID and the Google URL scheme.
//
// GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID
//   iOS OAuth client ID, e.g.
//   1234567890-abcdefghijklmnop.apps.googleusercontent.com
//   Must be the iOS client whose bundle ID is com.zefanya.app (or your
//   PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER).
//
// GOOGLE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID
//   The *web* OAuth client ID. Google puts it in the ID token's audience so
//   the Laravel backend can verify the token. Android also uses this value
//   via --dart-define=zefanya.googleServerClientId.
//
// GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID
//   The iOS client ID reversed, e.g.
//   com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abcdefghijklmnop
//   Google Sign-In uses it as the callback URL scheme. It must match
//   GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID exactly after reversing the host part.

GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID=
